From 029370ebe42a07ee9cc19aff55a1bb963c2c1504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:58:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: wait for both peers before checking disconnected GBT
 errors

disconnect_nodes waits for removal only at its first endpoint. The
remote socket handler may still retain a connection when the next
getblocktemplate RPC runs, so expecting RPC_CLIENT_NOT_CONNECTED
immediately on both nodes races with close propagation.

Explicitly disconnect and wait at the second endpoint with the existing
helper before asserting the unchanged -9 error on both nodes. This
changes only test synchronization, not RPC behavior, timeout values or
mempool diagnostics.

Test Plan: the actual unmodified test fails at its second-node assertion
when real TCP proxies delay FIN propagation by three seconds; this
version passes with the identical schedule. The before/after result
holds with upstream C++ binaries and a native Debug UBSan build. Ten
ordinary fixed-test UBSan repetitions pass. Original GitLab node logs
show the second RPC began before its final remote peer disconnected.
---
 test/functional/mining_getblocktemplate_errors.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/functional/mining_getblocktemplate_errors.py b/test/functional/mining_getblocktemplate_errors.py
index a0444db3d..d68e716d5 100755
--- a/test/functional/mining_getblocktemplate_errors.py
+++ b/test/functional/mining_getblocktemplate_errors.py
@@ -51,4 +51,6 @@ class GetBlockTemplateTest(BitcoinTestFramework):
         # and/or can't propagate blocks
         disconnect_nodes(self.nodes[0], self.nodes[1])
+        # The remote socket handler can observe disconnection later.
+        disconnect_nodes(self.nodes[1], self.nodes[0])
         assert_raises_rpc_error(-9, "Bitcoin is not connected!", self.nodes[0].getblocktemplate)
         assert_raises_rpc_error(-9, "Bitcoin is not connected!", self.nodes[1].getblocktemplate)
